================================================================================
PyMca (line-shape tail formula)
================================================================================

The opt-in low-energy tail of the EDS line shape (LineTail, Sources/SpectroEDX/Spectroscopy/Fit/EDSModel.swift) uses the
formula of PyMca's Hypermet short tail (PyMca, V. A. Sole et al., ESRF, MIT licence). The formula only; no PyMca code is
copied or ported.


================================================================================
HDF5 (through FormatoKit)
================================================================================

The Velox reader SpectroCore's spectrum-image opener calls is FormatoKit's FormatoEMD, which calls HDF5
(https://www.hdfgroup.org/, copyright The HDF Group and the Board of Trustees of the University of Illinois,
BSD-style license) through dlopen. Since SpectroKit 0.4.0 the libhdf5 a consumer gets is the one FormatoKit ships
inside FormatoHDF5 (HDF5 2.1.1 with libaec and libsz), unless the host supplies its own first; FormatoKit's NOTICE
carries those binaries' notice, checksums and license texts. SpectroKit itself neither links nor ships libhdf5.
